## Low / Info
- [dim 7] [lead B1] `task_self_update.c:1196` — `self_update_write_marker(state);` comes before the launch. A failed launch leaves the marker, so the next start shows a false "did not finish" report. Fix: write the marker after a successful `CreateProcessW`.
- [dim 7] [lead B2] `task_self_update.c:203-205` — a local failure to re-request is reported as "not yet available". Fix: route it to `self_update_check_failed(..., "request not started")`.
- [dim 7] [lead B3] `task_self_update.c:237-239` — a local version-parse failure is reported as "unreadable reply". Latent with the current `version.all`. Fix: give it a separate reason.
- [dim 7] [lead C1] `retroarch.c:5266` / `task_self_update.c:1415-1431` — the calloc, empty-staging and URL failures return false silently, and Update Now stays offered. Fix: notify and set DONE on those paths.
- [dim 7] NEW `menu_cbs_ok.c` `action_ok_self_update` — `task_push_self_update_check(false);` ignores its return. With "check at start-up" on, opening Update RetroArch while the quiet start-up check is still running gets refused by `self_update_check_running` (line 544).
  - Effect: no notification. The page shows the IDLE status with an empty line, so the user sees a blank page.
  - Fix: when the push returns false, set DONE with a "check already running" line, or let the quiet check be upgraded to a visible one.
- INFO: I did not open `self_update.c`, so `self_update_cleanup`'s name guard and `self_update_marker_consume` are taken from the header's description only. I did not check `frontend/drivers/platform_*.c` (the restart and installer hooks).
- Other dimensions, one line each:
  - **dim 2:** the divergences are the leads above. No other divergence from §4.5–§4.7 was found in the paths I read.
  - **dim 2b:** none. Update Now, the start-up check and the menu entry all have callers (`settings_def_self_update_action.h:19`, `retroarch.c:6845`, `menu_displaylist.c`).
  - **dim 3:** nothing found.
    - Member paths are fixed or filtered: `"new.AppImage"`, or through `self_update_program_member`, which rejects `..`.
    - The download name is `path_basename` of a URL built locally.
    - The certificate-checking gate is in both entry points (lines 548 and 1407).
    - A checksum other than 404 or 200 stops the update (lines 1376-1383), as INV-7 requires.
  - **dim 4:** nothing found.
  - **dim 5:** nothing found. Every error path I traced frees `state` exactly once.
  - **dim 8:**
    - The known http-task use-after-free trap is absent. No callback touches `task` beyond `task->state` in `cb_self_update_applied`, and that is its own task.
    - Each `user_data` is either handed on to a successful push or freed — I checked every failure branch.
    - The statics `buf` (line 1104) and `reason` (line 912) are used only by the worker-thread handler, and only one update can run at a time.
    - `self_update_set_status` runs only from main-thread callbacks.
  - **dim 9:** the AppImage file is fsynced before the rename (lines 1003-1007). The directory is not fsynced, but a lost rename leaves the old AppImage in place and staging is cleaned at the next start, so no data is lost. No finding.
  - **dim 10–15:** N/A, because no observability, portability, accessibility, localisation or privacy contract was named.
  - **dim 16:**
    - Network failure, download failure and cancellation all reach `self_update_apply_failed`.
    - A process killed mid-update leaves staging, and start-up cleanup removes it.
    - Nothing further was found beyond the leads.
  - **dim 17:** the marker has a format. An unparsable marker is removed according to the header, which I did not verify. The new setting defaults to false. Nothing found.

## Covered by spec and looks correct
I opened all of these and confirmed them against spec §4.5–§4.7, §6 and INV-5, -7, -13 and -14:
- `task_self_update.c` in full: the check chain, the apply chain, the order of the extract and install stages, the memory gate per block, and the checksum handling.
- The `retroarch.c` glue at lines 5260-5268 and 6838-6846.
- The `menu_displaylist.c` self-update list.
- The `Makefile.common` and `qb` gates.

## Open questions
- **The project rule and spec §4.1 disagree about griffin** (G1). Should the project contract's griffin rule carry the spec's "only for a target that can build it" exception? This is document-side, for `review-contract`.
- **Line 550:** on the quiet start-up check, the certificate-checking refusal still notifies (`self_update_notify(...TLS_REQUIRED)` runs whether or not `quiet` is set). That means one message per start. The check-failed path stays silent instead ("nobody asked", line 140). Spec §4.9 says the start-up check produces a notification only for a newer release, while §6 says the refusal "names the TLS setting". I cannot tell which applies to the quiet case.
- **Spec §4.6 installer step 2 writes the marker before run.cmd.** If B1 is fixed by moving the write, the spec's order changes too.

## 3 items to fix first
1. **B1:** the false "update did not finish" report after a failed installer launch. It is the only finding that tells the user something untrue about their install.
2. **C1:** the three silent `false` returns behind Update Now. The user presses a button, nothing happens, and the button stays.
3. **The new `action_ok_self_update` blank page.** It is reachable by anyone who has "check at start-up" on and opens the page early. The fix is one line.
